{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779478121,"nonce":"aIe9BpabpZZnoLzin3YRYKTxy8M=","message":"Updated framing from the recurrence/state review, relevant to the shared ValueSpec/function/distribution editor:\n\nKeep the backend split between port dataflow and `StateIndex` state. ValueSpec should not blur this by mutating Equinox module fields during a rollout. The scope matrix should be explicit in both schema and UX:\n\n- run sweep: may vary topology, component type, hidden size, static params, and presence/shape of ports or recurrent edges; resolves to a concrete graph/config before compile;\n- replicate/ensemble: may vary same-shape leaf values, sampled params, seeds, state initializers, and recurrent-edge initial values; compatible with vmap/static PyTree structure;\n- trial/episode: may vary reset-time values such as task params, initial state, and initial recurrent carries; shape-preserving within a compiled run;\n- timestep: may vary only as scanned dataflow: task signals, masks, control ports, intervention `params_override` inputs, or other explicit per-step arrays/functions. It is not module field mutation.\n\nUX consequence: a parameter/value field can accept a constant, expression, distribution, schedule, or sweep object, but the editor must know the field eligibility and selected scope. If the user tries a timestep schedule on a static/topological field, offer a promotion path such as \"make this a task/control signal\", \"target an intervention input\", or \"use this as a run sweep\" instead of silently accepting a backend-impossible object.\n\nThis makes recurrence and ValueSpec meet at two places: recurrent-edge initial values and state-slot initial values are valid replicate/trial scoped ValueSpecs; timestep-varying hidden/control dynamics should flow through ports/interventions or explicitly owned state updates, not through out-of-place mutation of Equinox module fields inside `lax.scan`.","files":null}]}